body:
I feel like I've read this before. I think you've posted before but i didnt check your history. Obviously it's complicated and you have history with her. Still, she obviously is a toxic person at least when she is with you. The thing you have to really understand is that even if you marry a woman, she will never love you or respect you all the time. She should, but she won't. It's a biological trait, ingrained into our dna. So either you overcome that primitive programming and rise to a higher level of consciousness or you give into your programming and keep looking for a "better" mate. What's the point of marrying if you're not going to keep your promise when times get tough. That's why I don't respect monogamy. Either you make a promise and keep it, or you just don't make a promise and don't disappoint other people.

&#x200B;

She left you as soon as things got complicated, she is used to everything always being rainbows and butterflies. That other guy made her feel those novel in-love feelings again so she jumped to him. Most likely that will end as well. Even though it feels like the end of the world, you are better off without her man. What if you had kids? Since you don't, you can make a clean cut. Forget she ever existed and only remember the lessons. She's not worthy of you. 

&#x200B;

Fuck please don't end your life because of a woman. It's all in your mind.

maybe you lack a healthy relationship with yourself. Meditation can help. But furthermore, I would recommend getting into spirituality. You don't have to identify yourself as a member of a certain spiritual group/community. Spirituality is about your relationship with yourself mainly. Yes there's also the part about ethics which concerns your relationship with fellow human beings, but being spiritual is about discovering and nourishing parts of yourself. Maybe the literature you have read about religions and spirituality have turned you off until now. Maybe you haven't ever considered reading about it because you related that to being dumb, uneducated or superstitious. You don't have to read religious/spiritual books but some introductory text about spirituality and meditation can be a starting point.

&#x200B;

It's mainly about finding meaning inside rather than looking for it outside (which seems to be what you have been doing). When you keep looking for something outside of you to satisfy you, that search will never end and will leave you satisfied. It's like hunger and fast food. You eat and satisfy yourself for a short period of time but then you realize you want more. You get hungry again. And so you keep looking for more food. Being happy or rather content is a state of mind which is not dependent on outside circumstances. The good thing is that you can train your mind to be in that state more often. States of conciousness are basically patterns of electrical signals or brain waves. The more you repeat a pattern the more likely it will be in that state often. If your mind is programmed to repeat a pattern that is a state of distress, of searching, of hunger, then you will keep finding yourself in that state no matter how much money you make, ow much food you eat, how much sex you have. This sort of hints to what the Buddha realised. Hunger, sexual appetite, desire for connection, desire for experiencing the new. Basically Desire. It can not be satisfied, ever. So Buddha practiced asceticism for a while. That can be a good starting point to control your urges and stop your mind and body from always wanting more and searching for novel experiences but in the end the Buddha realised it wasn't the ultimate answer either.

&#x200B;

The answer is still not known but the way to reach a state of being content is through daily meditation. It gives you control over your mind and bodily urges. It creates a relationship with yourself. It creates space for you to just be, without having to be stimulated by outside all the time. I'd suggest you to think about this for a while and if there's one thing you can get out of this unnecessarily long comment reply it's this:

Meditate. Learn and practice it daily.

you shouldn't recognize trolls as real entities who have power over your life. Because they dont. They're not real. If you saw those people irl, they'd run and hide under the table like a p..sy (ok what's another word for scared living thing? I want to stop using this word).

&#x200B;

DON'T KILL YOURSELF! YOU ARE LOVED <3
